  "notes": [
    "Source PDF: the genuine Fairchild Semiconductor (now onsemi) MOC301XM/MOC302XM Rev. 1.5 (July 2015) family datasheet, obtained via the componentsearchengine.com (SamacSys) mirror because onsemi.com and its direct mirrors (mouser, lcsc) were WAF-blocked/JS-gated at extraction time. The mirror is byte-identical to the manufacturer document for pages 1-9 and 13 (trademarks/disclaimer); page 14 is an appended Mouser distributor cover page and carries no device specifications. Page numbers in provenance are the printed Fairchild page numbers, which match this PDF's pages 1-9.",
    "Grade scope: this document describes only the MOC3021M grade (IFT max 15 mA, VDRM 400 V). The datasheet's IFT column also lists MOC3020M=30 mA, MOC3011M/MOC3022M=10 mA and MOC3012M/MOC3023M=5 mA; those are separate orderable grades and are intentionally not merged in (spec: one grade per document).",
    "Edge case - static dv/dt: this datasheet has NO guaranteed static dv/dt table row. A typical value of 10 V/us was read at TA=25 C off the Figure 7 characterization curve (dv/dt vs. Temperature, y-axis 0-12 V/us) and is stored with limitClass 'characterized' and a conditionsVerbatim note. The 100 V/us figure seen on Motorola-lineage MOC302x sheets does NOT appear on this onsemi/Fairchild PDF and was not used.",
    "Pinout: the datasheet labels both output pins (4 and 6) simply 'MAIN TERMINAL' and does not distinguish MT1 from MT2 (the bilateral switch is symmetric); both are given function MT. Pin 5 is the triac substrate, marked 'NC* - DO NOT CONNECT'.",
    "Non-numeric safety classifications (not modeled as values): Installation Classifications I-IV (for rated mains < 150 VRMS and < 300 VRMS), Climatic Classification 40/85/21, and Pollution Degree 2 (DIN VDE 0110/1.89), all page 2."
  ]
}
